      "claim": "The automatic half of `work land --again` can never fire in production. `returnedPathsResolved` (in the land command's lane code) requires the rebase to leave the branch at the returned commit (old tip = new tip = the returned commit) while also listing every returned conflict path in `Regenerated` or `Resolved`. The rebase fills `Regenerated` only when it replays the branch onto a newer main, which moves the tip, and nothing ever fills `Resolved`. The 'regenerated' and 'resolved' subtests build a rebase result the rebase cannot produce. The design's intent is still met another way: a return the rebase actually resolves leaves the branch at a new commit, which is handed in as a normal new hand-in with no `--again`. Without the fix the slice still works and is safe, so this is recorded and not acted on. It fits the design's 'later, when it hurts' list: remove the dead predicate and the `Resolved` field, or make the condition reachable when resolve-round (4b) starts setting `Resolved`.",
