      "claim": "`--again` re-queues any returned commit, including one a person returned with `landing return`, and the queue does not record who made the return. An agent's mistaken `--again` therefore puts a person's return back in line for another proof. This is what accepted Decision 5 specifies: whether the return 'needed no change' is the caller's judgement. The lane re-proves the commit and returns it again if it is still wrong. Before this change an agent could already get around the same-commit refusal by adding a trivial commit. This is not a breach of rulings R-142-m1e or R-143-m1e, whose list of a person's decisions does not include a return. The `landing return` help text still says only that 'a new commit ... is handed in again'.",
